     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\">Hello!</span>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\">I have fitted the tree detectability models to a dataset of visual records of resplendent quetzals in sampling transects in Guatemala. I want to extract detectability values and other values from the uniform\r\n model using the command summarize_ds_models(BQ.uni, output=&quot;plain&quot;). However, I&#39;m getting this error: &gt; summarize_ds_models(BQ.uni, output=&quot;plain&quot;) Error in\r\n</span><span style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;font-size:0.875em;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-weight:600;font-family:&quot;S\\0000f6hne Mono&quot;,Monaco,&quot;Andale Mono&quot;,&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,monospace\">[.data.frame</span><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\">(res,\r\n , 4:7) : undefined columns selected. </span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\">Could you help me resolve it?</span><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\">Thanks a lot!!</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\"><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"color:rgb(13,13,13);font-size:16px\"><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n<p></p></div></div>"
